            <ArticleTitle>Management of Pisotriquetral Instability.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0363-5023(17)30914-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jhsa.2017.10.020</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pisotriquetral instability is an often-overlooked condition that can lead to ulnar-sided wrist pain and dysfunction. Various case series and biomechanical studies have been published regarding the diagnosis and treatment of this condition. We review current methods for examining, diagnosing, and treating pisotriquetral instability.</AbstractText>
